<title>USA: ITT Hartford Q3 loss after charges.</title>
<headline>ITT Hartford Q3 loss after charges.</headline>
<dateline>HARTFORD, Conn. 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr	   loss     $ $4.63   profit	$ 1.48</p>
<p> Net	   loss     543,000   profit     173,000</p>
<p> Revs		   1,594,000		1,589,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 117,200		  117,100</p>
<p>	  NINEMONTHS</p>
<p> Shr	   loss    $  $2.59   profit	$ 3.57</p>
<p> Net	   loss     304,000   profit     418,000</p>
<p> Revs		   4,756,000		4,746,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 117,200		  117,100</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q3 results include $693 million in non-recurring after-tax charges. They comprise an increase in asbestos and environmental reserves of $510 million, acceleration of $169 million in future losses on the closed book of Guaranteed Investment Contracts, and other items totalling $14 million, mostly related to foreign taxes.</p>
<p>Without the charges, 1996 Q3 net would have been $150 million.</p>
<p>Full name is ITT Hartford Group Inc.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk, (212) 859-1610</p>
